{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789218625,"nonce":"u1YEQzUGNiH7o6sfTERCnAOygvE=","title":"A JIT rebuild left every loaded module but one without its globals","message":"rebuild_with_accumulated_symbols clears global_map; only current_module\nwas recompiled afterwards. Every earlier module kept code and lost the\naddresses of its globals, so a handler declared in the first file was\nuninstallable once the second loaded. finalize_runtime_symbols rebuilt\ndirectly and restored nothing, bypassing the one place that did.\n\nFixed: every loaded module is kept in load order and recompiled after a\nrebuild; the op table is resolved at install time rather than cached on\nthe instance. Kept by identity, not name: a host gives every file the\nsame module name. Reported by Blinc; confirmed resolved on their tests.","files":null}]}